Untangle kernel configuration overrides for Trixie 6.12.

Slimmed from the Bookworm-era 24-line patch. Removed lines that targeted
kernel symbols no longer carried in our patch series:

  IMQ + IMQ_BEHAVIOR_*  -> replaced by mainline IFB + tc mirred
  IP_NF_TUNE / IP6_NF_TUNE -> replaced by 'nft table inet tune'
  IP_NF_MATCH_BITMARK   -> replaced by native nft 'meta mark & 0xff'
  NFNETLINK_COPY_UNTANGLE_MODE, NF_CONNTRACK_DICT, NFT_DICT,
  IP_NF_FRAG_ACCEPT     -> tied to unported patches; no userspace
                           consumes them

Also removed PREEMPT_VOLUNTARY (Trixie default) and IP_ROUTE_MULTIPATH
(Trixie default) and UFS_FS (no NGFW use case).

Result: 8 effective overrides — HZ tuning, force core netfilter built-in,
and latency profiling.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/debian/config/featureset-untangle/config
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+##
+## file: kernel/Kconfig.hz
+##
+## choice: Timer frequency
+# CONFIG_HZ_250 is not set
+CONFIG_HZ_1000=y
+## end choice
+CONFIG_HZ=1000
+
+##
+## file: net/netfilter/Kconfig
+##
+# Force core netfilter built-in to eliminate boot-time modprobe races.
+# UVM, sync-settings, and all rule-loading scripts assume these are
+# present unconditionally before any iptables/nft rules are loaded.
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_NETLINK=y
+CONFIG_NF_CONNTRACK=y
+CONFIG_NF_NAT=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XTABLES=y
+
+##
+## file: lib/Kconfig.debug
+##
+# Latency profiling support (/proc/latency_stats). Low overhead.
+CONFIG_LATENCYTOP=y
